# With Exalted Sunborn out, Royal Treatment's one Royal Role becomes two (CR 614.1a, 111.1), both created attached to
# the targeted creature, here the Sunborn itself. They are the same player's two Roles on one permanent, so the
# state-based action keeps one and puts the other into the graveyard (CR 704.5z; the Role rulings: of two that arrive
# together the player keeps one - two copies of one token, so either is the same game). The Sunborn is a 5/6, not a 6/7.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Exalted Sunborn
Royal Treatment
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Exalted Sunborn.Cast(Ability: Warp)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Royal Treatment.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Exalted Sunborn)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Jet; Mox Emerald; Exalted Sunborn; Royal
Bot1.Battlefield.Royal.AttachedTo = Exalted Sunborn
Bot1.Battlefield.Exalted Sunborn.Power = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Exalted Sunborn.Toughness = 6
LeftBattlefield = Royal
